WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 009, en. Timings estimated from the script until the clip is rendered (re-split 27 Oct 2026: <=2x42 chars, <=20 cps, <=180 wpm).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.467
<v I_NIA>Eighteen forty-one.
The tithe men come to Llandough.

2
00:00:03.587 --> 00:00:06.394
<v I_NIA>What did they write down about Tŷ Mawr?

3
00:00:10.814 --> 00:00:12.568
<v Amy Williams>[in Welsh] Bore da, John.

4
00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:15.846
<v Amy Williams>The tithe men left a
copy of their schedule.

5
00:00:15.966 --> 00:00:20.633
<v Amy Williams>Llandough, Cogan and Leckwith,
and your name down the occupier column,

6
00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:22.053
<v Amy Williams>over and over.

7
00:00:22.473 --> 00:00:23.773
<v Amy Williams>Thirty-six parcels.

8
00:00:23.893 --> 00:00:28.626
<v Amy Williams>Thirty-three are Bute land: a hundred
and nineteen acres, nought roods,

9
00:00:28.746 --> 00:00:30.046
<v Amy Williams>six perches.

10
00:00:30.166 --> 00:00:35.033
<v Amy Williams>Three little ones are glebe, church
land: two roods, twenty-four perches.

11
00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:40.586
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>Add them and you get a hundred and
nineteen acres, two roods, thirty perches.

12
00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:44.916
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>Every field I walk, written
down by a man with a chain.

13
00:00:45.336 --> 00:00:50.600
<v Amy Williams>And not a word about a lease,
or a term, or what rent we pay.

14
00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.825
<v Amy Williams>It shows who farms which field.

15
00:00:52.945 --> 00:00:54.348
<v Amy Williams>That's all it shows.

16
00:00:54.768 --> 00:00:57.835
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>They'll finish the plan
next year, 'forty- two,

17
00:00:57.955 --> 00:01:00.422
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>and it'll lie with the parish papers.

18
00:01:00.542 --> 00:01:04.942
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>Whether these fields are number
nineteen on the 'twenty-four plan,

19
00:01:05.062 --> 00:01:06.465
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>it won't tell you.

20
00:01:06.885 --> 00:01:10.043
<v Amy Williams>Nor where the hedges
will run in thirty years.

21
00:01:10.163 --> 00:01:12.630
<v Amy Williams>Paper moves slower than hedges, John.

22
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:21.316
<v Gwen>Twenty-third of December, and the
house quiet as the churchyard.

23
00:01:21.436 --> 00:01:23.103
<v Gwen>Sixty-five she was, John.

24
00:01:23.223 --> 00:01:25.223
<v Gwen>Sixty-five, here in Llandough.

25
00:01:25.643 --> 00:01:30.110
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>She kept this kitchen through the
tithe men and every winter since.

26
00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.363
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>I'll not have her written small.

27
00:01:32.783 --> 00:01:38.046
<v Gwen>The paper will print her the way it
prints widows: 'relict of the late Mr.

28
00:01:38.166 --> 00:01:42.433
<v Gwen>John Williams, Great House farm.'
The farm's own name, in print.

29
00:01:42.853 --> 00:01:47.120
<v John Williams: the c.1841 tithe occupier>Great House. Tŷ Mawr. Whatever
the estate calls it in its books.

30
00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.940
<v Gwen>Cardiff Times, sixteenth
of July, nineteen-oh-four.

31
00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.393
<v Gwen>John Williams, 'of Llandough Farm'.

32
00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:58.425
<v Gwen>And here: 'He succeeded his father in
the occupancy of the farm in 1855.'

33
00:01:58.845 --> 00:02:02.003
<v Gwen>Mind what it gives you
and what it doesn't.

34
00:02:02.123 --> 00:02:04.990
<v Gwen>Llandough Farm, it prints,
not Great House.

35
00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:10.443
<v Gwen>That he's the Great House John is our own
reckoning, matched against the census,

36
00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.030
<v Gwen>not the paper's words.

37
00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.257
<v Gwen>Father to son in one line of print.

38
00:02:15.377 --> 00:02:19.236
<v Gwen>No word of when the father
went, nor what he left.

39
00:02:19.356 --> 00:02:22.865
<v Gwen>Only that in 'fifty-five
the son took the farm on.
